      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T18:47:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Dai,\nAgree that for devices running with older ectool, it wont print.\nBut, the command(cmd_pwm_get_fan_rpm)  which uses this print doesnt depend on ec host command  to read rpm, but is reading rpm from memory location and printing it.So, i don\u0027t think, we have a way to verify the command version and then to decide about the stall print. In a way,rpm \u003d 0 gives same hint to user, eventhough  the stall print gets missed in boards with old fw.  Also,the moment when rpm is set to 0 in pwm_fan_second(), stall print will appear in ec log. So, it doesnt really impact boards with older fw.",
      "parentUuid": "22a4bbad_59c72e36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 32
